    \ </file>\n  <file path=\"tools/record-result/README.md\">\n    # Record Result\n
    \   \n    Record Result is a Go program that runs a given command, creates a git
    commit with the command that generated it, and saves it in the git metadata/note.\n
    \   \n    ## Installation\n    \n    1. Ensure you have Go installed on your system.\n
    \   2. Clone this repository:\n       ```\n       git clone https://github.com/yourusername/record-result.git\n
    \      ```\n    3. Change to the project directory:\n       ```\n       cd record-result\n
    \      ```\n    4. Build the program:\n       ```\n       go build\n       ```\n
    \   \n    ## Usage\n    \n    Run the program with the following syntax:\n    \n
    \   ```\n    ./record-result -- <command> [args...]\n    ```\n    \n    The program
    will:\n    1. Run the specified command\n    2. Create a git commit with all changes\n
    \   3. Add a git note with the command used\n    \n    Make sure you're in a git
    repository when running the program.\n    \n    Example:\n    ```\n    ./record-result
    -- echo \"Hello, World!\"\n    ```\n    \n    This will run the `echo \"Hello,
    World!\"` command, create a git commit with any changes, and add a git note with
    the command.\n    \n    ## License\n    \n    This project is licensed under the
    MIT License. See the [LICENSE](LICENSE) file for details.\n    \n  </file>\n  <file
    path=\"tools/record-result/go.mod\">\n    module record-result\n    \n    go 1.22.0\n
    \   \n    toolchain go1.22.4\n    \n    require github.com/tmc/langchaingo v0.1.12\n
    \   \n    require (\n    \tgithub.com/dlclark/regexp2 v1.10.0 // indirect\n    \tgithub.com/google/uuid
    v1.6.0 // indirect\n    \tgithub.com/pkoukk/tiktoken-go v0.1.6 // indirect\n    )\n
    \ </file>\n  <file path=\"tools/record-result/go.sum\">\n    github.com/davecgh/go-spew
